  "details": "Currently, an Avatar is either private (only uploader can use it) or public (anyone who find it can use it).  VRC has already established the concepts of alternative restrictions when it comes to world instances. It would make perfect sense to continue that design language to avatar sharing, especially now that sharing is a feature set.\n\nFriends only avatar would only be wearable/clonable by friends of the user who uploaded it.\n\nInvite only avatars would only be wearable/clonable by users designated by the user who uploaded it.\n\nGroup only avatars would only be wearable/clonable by users in a group designated by the uploaded when enabling this flag.",
